    [module name=ws       gate=enforced reason='IMPLEMENTED — the Ring 1 PURE WebSocket FRAME CODEC (spec/03-approved/stdlib/ws.md; #1086/#1461, RULED: INT-17, INT-19, 1430-e) lands with stdlib/ws.cx and vcx/code/stdlib_ws.v, so the 54 cases the corpus carried BEFORE the code are graded here. The corpus is hermetic and every one of the eleven public defs is Ring 1 and PURE — one RFC 6455 frame encoded and decoded with the octet count it consumed, a buffer read into its frames and the remainder it could not complete, the masking transform, fragmentation and assembly, the three control frames, the close body read into its code and reason, the UTF-8 rule a TEXT message carries, and the handshake accept value — so no case carries a grant=, a port or a store URL, and none reaches cx-platform/net or cx-platform/http: the connection and the upgrade EXCHANGE are http.md §3.7\'s. ws-001..015 are the FIFTEEN ATTACK CLASSES of the spec §5.1 and come first, 020..029 the framing and its three length forms, 030..034 the masking transform, 040..046 fragmentation and assembly, 050..056 the control frames and the close codes, 060..063 the UTF-8 rule, 070..072 the accept derivation and 080..082 the bounds at their edges. Every octet string is RFC 6455 §5.7\'s own worked example. Twelve codes are allocated, CXER6900..CXER6911 inside the band governance.md §9.6 registers for this module']
